# API Route Patterns

Routes are thin wrappers — all logic belongs in `@/features/*/services`.

```typescript
import { NextRequest, NextResponse } from "next/server";
import { createThing, listThings } from "@/features/things/services";

export async function GET() {
  try {
    const items = await listThings();
    return NextResponse.json(items);
  } catch (error) {
    return NextResponse.json(
      { message: error instanceof Error ? error.message : "Unable to load things." },
      { status: 500 },
    );
  }
}

export async function POST(request: NextRequest) {
  try {
    const body = await request.json();
    const item = await createThing(body);
    return NextResponse.json(item, { status: 201 });
  } catch (error) {
    return NextResponse.json(
      { message: error instanceof Error ? error.message : "Unable to create thing." },
      { status: 400 },
    );
  }
}
```

## Conventions

- Import services from feature barrels (`@/features/{feature}/services`)
- Return `{ message: string }` on errors; use `error instanceof Error`
- Use 201 for creates, 400 for validation/business errors, 500 for unexpected failures
- Respect `AppError.status` when catching domain errors
- REST naming: `GET/POST` collection, `GET/PATCH` resource, action routes as `POST .../activate`, `POST .../close`
